# Pinned tracebloc/data-ingestors commit the CLI's embedded schema (and, when
# the goldens drift job lands, the validator goldens) are synced from. CI
# checks against THIS ref, not a floating branch — so an unrelated upstream
# commit can't red every open CLI PR (backend#1009).
#
# To adopt upstream changes: bump this SHA, then run `scripts/sync-schema.sh`
# (and `scripts/sync-validator-goldens.sh` once its CI job exists) and commit
# the regenerated files together in one deliberate PR.
#
# Format: the first non-comment, non-blank line is the ref (a full commit SHA
# preferred; a branch name works but reintroduces floating drift).
#
# CURRENT PIN: tracebloc/data-ingestors PR #552 head (backend#1006 — drop
# labels.csv for object_detection). Previous pin was 8f89aece, develop HEAD as
# of 2026-07-14.
#
# ⚠️  THIS IS AN UNMERGED FEATURE-BRANCH COMMIT. It is pinned here so this PR's
# schema-check is green and reviewable against the real upstream file. BEFORE
# THIS PR MERGES, re-pin to the data-ingestors develop SHA that carries the
# #552 merge and re-run scripts/sync-schema.sh. Merging with a feature-branch
# pin would leave the CLI vendoring a schema that exists on no permanent ref.
#
# ⚠️  AND #552 IS NOT THE WHOLE STORY. It changed `ingest.v1.json` but left
# `layout.v1.json` still declaring a `labels_csv` manifest for object_detection,
# so data-ingestors contradicted itself and this vendored copy inherited the
# wrong half. Reported by @LukasWodka reviewing this PR; fixed by
# data-ingestors#556, which regenerates the contract at version 4 with
# `"manifest": null`.
#
# `internal/schema/layout.v1.json` here has ALREADY been updated to that v4
# content — the file is GENERATED from the ModalitySpec flags, so its bytes are
# deterministic and the only thing that has to wait for the merge is this SHA.
# The two-line diff against the old vendored copy is exactly #556's two changes
# and nothing else, verified by diff.
#
# So the re-pin below must land on the develop SHA carrying BOTH #552 and #556.
# Landing #552's alone would re-vendor the self-contradictory schema and quietly
# revert the fix. Order, per data-ingestors' own contract-consumers gate:
#   1. e2e-test-agent#428  — the consumer that refuses an unknown version
#   2. backend#3117        — sidecar-enumerated dataset generation
#   3. data-ingestors#556  — publish v4
#   4. THIS PR             — re-pin + re-sync
#
# What this bump adopts beyond #1006 — the pin was 7 weeks stale, so the
# re-sync necessarily brings these along (each verified against the CLI's own
# suite, see the PR body):
#   ff77a7d di#360  uploader-declared unit/ordinal descriptors (enriched schema)
#   913dd7a di#350  default data_id strategy uuid -> content_hash
#   36d2c72 di#360  top-level alignment facts settable from ingest.yaml
#   ed2d051 di#535  time-ordering constraint surfaced in layout.v1.json
#   b6f950f #1006   object_detection: no csv/label, records from Pascal-VOC XML
